To All,

Awhile back I posted about some Oracle performance problems when
going from 5.1a PK4 to 5.1a PK6 on our cluster. Below is the solution
that we found...


 > > Oracle 8.1.7 automatically opens all AdvFS (and CFS) files 
 > within the 
 > > database with the O_DIRECTIO flag if the RDBMS is running on Tru64 
 > > V5.0A and above. 
 > > There are some performance impact due to possible bugs in 
 > Direct IO.  
 > > 
 > > Fix:
 > > ~~~~ 
 > > Check nm $ORACLE_HOME/bin/oracle | grep tru64  
 > > It will return a row similar to 
 > > tru64_directio_disabled          | 0000005369947296 | S | 
 > > 0000000000000000 
 > > This shows oracle executable is capable of disabling the Direct IO 
 > > 
 > > If above command does not return any row then apply 8.1.7.2
 > > (or above) 
 > > patchset 
 > > to make it capable to disable the Direct IO. 
 > > 
 > > Then set _TRU64_DIRECTIO_DISABLED=TRUE in init.ora and bounce the
 > > database. 
 > > 
 > > References:
 > > ~~~~~~~~~~~ 
 > > [NOTE:132391.1] Direct IO on Tru64 UNIX V5.0A and V5.1 

Setting _TRU64_DIRECTIO_DISABLED=TRUE for all databases on our cluster
brought index build performance back to normal.

Also, we had already done this, but Oracle/HP recommends...


 > > For 5.1a patchkit 4 or greater is required.
 > > You must also edit the following parameters in the
 > > /etc/sysconfigtab file:
 > >   vm: new_wire_method = 0
 > >   vfs: fifo_do_adaptive = 0

I have one minor complaint about this whole process. We had checked
with both HP and Oracle before the patch kit upgrade to see if there
would be any issues. Both said no. Also, the follow-up with both
Oracle and HP did not resolve this issue. We had to go to user groups
to find the above solution. Its not very reassuring when neither Oracle
or HP could give us the fix when both parties obviously had to make a
fix explicitly for this upgrade.

