Hi,

You should use the sysman Audit Manager (sysman applications ->
Daily Administration -> Audit Manager) aka /usr/tcb/bin/dxaudit or
the auditmask command to set up audit object selection.  See the
V5.1B Security Administration guide section 3.4.6 "Auditing
File Operations" and/or the auditmask man page, paying particular
attention to the options: -q -Q -s -x -X.  Note that you have to
enable the obj_sel style characteristic for object selection to be
enabled.  Running auditmask without options will show you your
current audit mask including style characteristics.  From your info
below, it looks like object selection is off.

Ann

