To All Tru64 Wizards,

We have a Tru64 cluster with the following recent issue:

Since going from 5.1a PK4 to PK6, we have been experiencing significant
Oracle slowdowns. The slowdowns can be attributes to the patch kit as
nightly processing was consistent before the upgrade and has increased
immediately afterwards.

The Oracle slowdowns are very limited in scope. In particular, primarily
Oracle 8.1.7.2.1 databases are affected and only index builds for those
databases. Other database processing has stayed within normal run times.
The average increase in run times for database index rebuilds is between
3 and 5 times longer than historical averages - for instance, one rebuild
job went from an average run time of 25 minutes to 85. This is typical of
what we're now seeing for all Oracle 8.1.7.2.1 databases.

Index builds of Oracle 9i databases have been less affected with run
time increases of about 50%. All other 9i activity has been normal.

Oracle databases are the only applications running on this Tru64 cluster.
The only other activity is nightly backups and those run times have not
changed since the install of patch kit 6. So, it appears to be isolated
to particular Oracle activities, but the application set is limited.

So far, investigation has shown that no changes of any kind have taken
place other than the patch kit 6 installation. All system parameters are
the same. All filesystems are being served by the same cluster members as
before. No database tuning changes have occurred. No system resource
starvation (as shown by collect) is evident as these systems have plenty
of idle cpu and memory, and I/O characteristics have not changed.

We are persuing the issue with Oracle, but would like to hear of any
similar experiences at other Tru64 sites that have gone to patch kit 6.

FYI: Without going into detail, the cluster specifics are
        Tru64 5.1a Patch Kit 6
        5 members (3 GS80s, 2 DS20s)
        SAN consists of EVA5000 & EMA12000 

Thanx in advance.
