I am porting my 'c' application to a Tru64 system, uname output follows;

OSF1 nodeX V5.1 1885 alpha

I have found two make commands, one in /sbin (symbolic link to /bin) the 
other in /usr/bin/posix.

I have observation and two questions.  My observation is that the 
/sbin/make does not seem to handle typical dependents such as;

.c.o:
	cc ...

.c.a:	
	cc ...
	ar ...

lib.a:	lib.a(module.o)

What I find is that /sbin/make wants to run the .c.o rule instead of the 
.c.a rule.  Does anyone know what standards the /sbin/make conforms too?

The second question is will a base Tru64 system always have 
/usr/bin/posix/make? This make works fine with my Makefile, but, I 
typically am granted access to customer's systems for any enhancements 
and changes.  I want to know if I should keep a copy of the 
/usr/bin/posix/make or if it will always be available on other Tru64 
systems?



