As I recall, for backwards compatibility, we could not replace the
current make(3) with the POSIX make as this could break the building of
many applications. I believe that the /bin/make (or /sbin/make) is the
BSD version of make. There should be a blurb in the release notes about
this. I think this goes back to version 3.0. 

